    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Constants (plain numbers) stay separate from x-terms. Simplify each group on its own: 4n + 3 + 2n = (4n+2n) + 3 = 6n + 3.",
      "figure": "tse-combine-like"
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Combine like terms, keep the constant.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "mcq",
        "prompt": "Simplify: 4n + 3 + 2n",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "6n + 3",
            "correct": true,
            "feedback": "Yes — combine the n-terms (4n+2n=6n), the +3 stays separate."
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "6n",
            "feedback": "Don't drop the constant — it has no matching term, so it stays: 6n + 3."
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "9n",
            "feedback": "The +3 isn't an n-term — it can't combine with 4n or 2n. Keep it separate: 6n + 3."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "You can distribute first, then combine — 2(x+3)+4x becomes 2x+6+4x, and combining the x-terms gives 6x+6.",
